summary:
  A delay set by hand is written to the map without a word in the journal.

history:
  The delay map has four writers, and this was the only one of them that
  said nothing. On 2026-11-11 the map went from 181 to 161 ninety seconds
  after a panel restart. The journal showed a correction landing and the
  next probe working with 161, and no line between them to say who had
  asked for it; the room then read 21, 27 and 20 ms out for ten minutes
  before the settle put it back. The hand was found by ruling out the
  three writers that do speak. Two notches of the wheel over the slider
  are enough to do it.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SyncJournal.js

find:
      if (_same(was, now)) return "";

replace:
      return "";

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_sync_journal.py::test_a_delay_set_by_hand_leaves_one_line_with_the_map_before_and_after.
  Line-neutral.
